# The Prisma CLI resolves .env relative to its working directory, and `pnpm --filter
# @skillwright/db <script>` runs with the cwd set to this package. Copy this file to
# packages/db/.env (or export DATABASE_URL in the shell) before running migrations.
#
# PORT 5433, not 5432. docker-compose.yml publishes Postgres on ${POSTGRES_PORT:-5433}
# because a native Postgres owns 5432 on the machine this was built on, and the root
# .env.example agrees. This file said 5432 until 2026-08-30, so a fresh clone that
# copied it connected to whatever was on 5432 — usually nothing, occasionally someone
# else's database. Override POSTGRES_PORT in the root .env if you want the standard
# port, and change this line to match.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://skillwright:skillwright@localhost:5433/skillwright?schema=public"

# NO ENCRYPTION KEY HERE. This file used to declare TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY, alongside a
# comment claiming "the API must read the same variable or that admin cannot complete
# MFA" — and the API read ENCRYPTION_KEY, from the ROOT .env, in a different format.
# The comment was right about the consequence and wrong about the variable, so the
# seeded MFA admin rejected every correct code it was ever given.
#
# The seed now encrypts through encryptTotpSecret (packages/db/src/totp.ts), which
# reads ENCRYPTION_KEY from the repository-root .env — the same key, the same file and
# the same envelope apps/api decrypts with. Copy the root .env.example to .env and
# there is nothing to set here. apps/api/test/auth.test.ts fails if they ever diverge.
